From: sheng-development <sheng-development@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 17:45:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Discover the SSC accelerometer first

find_sensors() walks drivers[] in order and each SSC discovery blocks until it
finishes, so a driver placed early holds up every driver behind it. Upstream
lists the SSC drivers as proximity, light, accel, compass, which puts the
accelerometer third.

That ordering is what makes auto-rotate wait on sensors it does not need. Now
that libssc retries a data type the aDSP has not registered yet, proximity
spends its whole retry budget when the hardware has nothing to offer, and the
accelerometer sits behind it.

Nothing here depends on discovery order, so put the accelerometer first and
leave the sensors that may have to wait until last.
---
 src/iio-sensor-proxy.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
index 3ac9052..795b33d 100644
--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
@@ -80,10 +80,10 @@ static const SensorDriver * const drivers[] = {
 	&iio_poll_proximity,
 	&input_proximity,
 #ifdef HAS_LIBSSC
-	&ssc_proximity,
-	&ssc_light,
 	&ssc_accel,
 	&ssc_compass,
+	&ssc_light,
+	&ssc_proximity,
 #endif
 };
 
